{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"06887ac4-97a0-4b79-91fe-ba8e3c274b20","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Root Cause\n\nIn Flutter, PostHog mobile session replay relies on `PostHogWidget` wrapping the root application widget (`MaterialApp` / `MaterialApp.router` / `CupertinoApp`) to capture UI frames/screenshots. \n\nWhile events, screen transitions, and taps continued to arrive via `PosthogObserver` and analytics tracking calls:\n- [`LegacyApp`](file:///tmp/h-Np2Abb/lib/legacy_app.dart#L13-L23) wrapped its `MaterialApp` in `PostHogWidget`, so session replay worked as expected for users on the old UI.\n- [`NewApp`](file:///tmp/h-Np2Abb/lib/new_app.dart#L24-L31) was missing the `PostHogWidget` wrapper around its `MaterialApp.router`. Without it, no visual frames were captured or sent to PostHog, resulting in empty recordings.\n\n### Fix\n\nWrapped `MaterialApp.router` in `PostHogWidget` in [`lib/new_app.dart`](file:///tmp/h-Np2Abb/lib/new_app.dart#L24-L34) and documented the explanation in [`ANSWER.md`](file:///tmp/h-Np2Abb/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":94.87613,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":156297,"output_tokens":2083,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":199373,"total_tokens":158380}}}
